WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:32.533
[ Music ]

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:38.066
[Narrator:] This is Grand Rapids, Michigan, a town becoming widely known to dentists

00:00:38.066 --> 00:00:42.666
and municipal authorities...against tooth decay.

00:00:42.666 --> 00:00:48.732
The children in Grand Rapids have less tooth decay than they did six years ago,

00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:55.233
as much as 65 percent less.

00:00:55.233 --> 00:01:00.333
Grand Rapids' fight against tooth decay started in January 1945,

00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:06.866
when fluoride was added to the water supply.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:13.666
This was done as part of a study to determine the effect of fluoridation on tooth decay.

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:20.132
Participating in the study are city officials, dentists, Michigan State Department of Health,

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:24.133
University of Michigan, and the U.S. Public Health Service.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:30.599
After six years of fluoridation, the study shows that the six-year-old children who drank the water

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:40.100
from birth had 65 percent less tooth decay, the seven-year-olds, 45 percent less, and so on.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.940
Even the 16-year olds who started drinking the water when they were 10 years old

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.440
received some benefits; 16 percent less tooth decay.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.320
Sixteen years after fluoridation all children, 16 years old and under,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.300
will have 65 percent less tooth decay.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:12.599
Studies in Newburgh, New York; Sheboygan, Wisconsin; Marshall, Texas; Lewiston, Idaho;

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:18.000
Brantford, Ontario, and other cities, show substantially the same results

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.133
as those obtained at Grand Rapids.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:25.873
Other studies show the benefits of fluoridation will last throughout life.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:38.060
Most of the many communities now fluoridating add sodium silico-fluoride

00:02:38.066 --> 00:02:41.499
or sodium fluoride to their water.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:48.300
Another compound also used is hydrofluosilicic acid. All three are effective and cheap.

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:59.433
In a town of 5,000 population, the daily amount of the fluoride compound used and its cost is:

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:07.666
Sodium silico-fluoride, seven pounds, cost 49 cents.

00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:15.699
Sodium chloride, 10 pounds, cost one dollar, 20 cents.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:22.166
Hydrofluosilicic acid, about two gallons, one dollar, sixty-one cents.

00:03:22.166 --> 00:03:29.026
In selecting one of the three compounds, the size of the town and its water plant facilities are considered.

00:03:32.466 --> 00:03:36.966
Three types of feeders are used to add fluoride compounds.

00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:42.326
One is the solution feeder, used in towns up to about 20,000 population.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:51.953
Another type is the volumetric feeder; a dry feeder for towns of from 1,000 to 120,000.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:04:01.146
The third type is the gravimetric feeder, for feeding the dry compound in cities of more than 120,000.

00:04:03.433 --> 00:04:09.966
All three feeders--the solution feeder, the volumetric feeder and the gravimetric--

00:04:09.966 --> 00:04:13.899
are equipped with automatic controls and have long been used

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.560
for adding chemicals to city water supplies.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:24.540
Generally, the fluoride content of the water is determined by the color metric test.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:32.866
In this test, a color indicator is added to water samples.

00:04:32.866 --> 00:04:37.386
The color of the samples is then matched with the color of standards

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.080
containing known amounts of fluoride.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:49.833
Dentists in many cities are helping to bring the benefits of fluoridation to children.

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:54.793
Now, our children can have better health through fluoridated water.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:04.120
They can drink away tomorrow's tooth decay, have more attractive teeth.

00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:11.799
The cost is about ten cents a year per person.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:15.333
[ Music ]

00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:20.499
Fluoridation is endorsed by the American Dental Association,

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:26.300
state and territorial dental health directors, American Association of Public Health Dentists,

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.680
Public Health Service, Federal Security Agency,

00:05:30.366 --> 00:05:35.326
state and territorial health officers, American Public Health Association,

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.933
and the American Medical Association.

00:05:38.933 --> 00:05:46.453
[ Music ]

